's choice. At this moment the game was nearly even, and it was GPT-6.1 Sol's chance to take over."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's E3 was the worst move of the game: 16.1 points lost, from -0.2 to -16.3. The engine wanted E8. The even game was gone in one move, and White's lead stayed large from then on."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's J6 lost 12.3 points (-26.3 → -38.6), with B2 as the engine's choice. The 20k's reply J8 lost 12.2 points (-38.6 → -26.4), so most of the damage was handed back, but White was still far ahead."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script only inspects the current board or records: the `inspect` function (command 4) lists existing chains, liberties and empty regions, and for the one move the player names it shows the resulting chain and any captures. The rest parses the move log, replays the actual moves to check the final board, writes the SGF and review files, and calls the play tool. Nothing loops over candidate moves or plays continuations forward, so there is no search.", "stop": false}}